abstract: "This paper presents an open-source Python suite for sparse three-dimensional displacement tracking and kinematic analysis in large-scale structural dynamic experiments. The suite consists of five tools. Three utility tools handle upstream preparation: VidTrim trims raw video footage to the required size with lossless FFmpeg encoding; tkCalib2 derives camera parameters from either checkerboard image sets or single-image control-point correspondences; and TempArUco uses ArUco fiducial markers to generate template files for stereo cameras automatically. ParaStereoSync performs CPU-parallelized enhanced correlation coefficient (ECC) image tracking, sub-frame temporal synchronization by reprojection-error minimization, and stereo triangulation; and KineViz-3D provides interactive 3D heatmap visualization, profile evolution dashboards, phase-space trajectory analysis, automated peak-misalignment detection, and six-degree-of-freedom rigid body decomposition. Demonstrated on shake-table testing of suspended ceiling systems with 324 simultaneously tracked spatial nodes, the suite delivers a complete pipeline from raw video to quantified structural kinematics using only consumer-grade cameras and standard Python scientific libraries."
